ining,Sandy,Loamy,Poor}', 'Eastern North America', 90, 120, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/4096046/square.JPG', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/4096046/medium.JPG', true, 129315, 129315, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera bocatorensis', 'Monstera bocatorensis', 6.0, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Insoluble calcium oxalate crystals cause oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs if ingested.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings. Water thoroughly when top layer feels dry to touch.', 60, 80, 'Intermediate', 'A tropical climbing aroid with deeply lobed or fenestrated leaves, smaller and more compact than Monstera deliciosa. Prized as a houseplant for its architectural foliage and air-purifying qualities in moderate light conditions.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Contains insoluble calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes mouth and throat irritation, excessive salivation, and difficulty swallowing. Skin contact may cause mild dermatitis.', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Moderate', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central America (Honduras, Costa Rica)', 150, 60, true, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/170642058/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/170642058/medium.jpeg', true, 1639758, 1639758, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera wilsoniensis', 'Monstera wilsoniensis', 6.0, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings; water thoroughly when the top inch feels dry to touch.', 60, 80, 'Intermediate', 'A rare and compact aroid species with deeply pinnate or lobed leaves, prized by collectors for its distinctive foliage pattern. Slower-growing and more delicate than common Monsteras, requiring consistent warmth and humidity.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral and throat irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing. Sap may cause skin irritation.', false, NULL, true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Slow', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central America (endemic to a limited region; exact native range poorly documented)', 90, 60, true, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/109073480/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/109073480/medium.jpeg', true, 1387024, 1387024, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera lamersiana', 'Monstera lamersiana', 6.0, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings. Check soil moisture at the surface before watering.', 60, 80, 'Intermediate', 'A rare, climbing aroid with deeply fenestrated or lobed leaves, similar to Monstera deliciosa but with smaller, more densely patterned foliage. Prized by collectors for its compact growth habit and air-purifying qualities in indoor spaces.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Sap and leaves contain calcium oxalate crystals, causing oral burning, irritation of the mouth and throat, and potential difficulty swallowing if ingested. Skin contact may cause mild irritation.', false, NULL, true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central America (Mexico and Guatemala)', 180, 60, true, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/215201426/square.jpg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/215201426/medium.jpg', true, 1544463, 1544463, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Antitrichia curtipendula', 'Pendulous wing-moss', 5.0, 7.5, false, '{Division}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 15:02:20.60003+00', NULL, 'Frequent', '{part_shade,filtered_indirect}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Keep substrate consistently moist but not waterlogged; check moisture at surface regularly. Mosses do not have traditional root systems and absorb water directly.', 70, 100, 'Intermediate', 'A delicate, pendulous moss species with feathery fronds that form cascading tufts, native to temperate regions. Prized in terrarium cultivation and as an epiphyte on tree bark for its elegant, trailing growth pattern.', 'Both', false, false, NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Slow', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Peaty,Moisture-retaining}', 'Temperate regions of Northern Hemisphere, including Europe and North America', NULL, NULL, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/7266920/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/7266920/medium.jpg', true, 126107, 126107, 'species');
