pale pink or white flowers. Native to damp meadows and grasslands, it thrives in cool, moist conditions and is valued for naturalized plantings and wildlife gardens.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, true, 'Late Spring – Early Summer', true, 'Spring', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Loamy,Moisture-retaining,Rich}', 'Europe and temperate Asia', 60, 30, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/601068973/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/601068973/medium.jpg', true, 54531, 54531, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera juliusii', 'Monstera juliusii', 6.0, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral irritation, swelling of mouth and throat, difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings. Check soil moisture at this depth; water thoroughly when dry at touch.', 60, 80, 'Intermediate', 'A rare tropical aroid with deeply lobed or fenestrated leaves and robust climbing or trailing growth habit. Prized by collectors for its distinctive foliage and moderate air-purifying capacity; slower-growing than Monstera deliciosa but equally striking indoors.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Sap and foliage contain calcium oxalate crystals; skin contact may cause dermatitis or irritation. Ingestion causes oral pain, swelling, and difficulty swallowing.', false, NULL, true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central America', 180, 90, true, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/397951498/square.jpg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/397951498/medium.jpg', true, 1639750, 1639750, 'species');
