ng,Loamy}', 'Hong Kong, Southern China', 150, 120, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/261732926/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/261732926/medium.jpeg', true, 543398, 543398, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera tuberculata', 'Giant monstera', 6.0, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings. Check soil moisture at the surface before watering.', 60, 80, 'Intermediate', 'A large-leaved tropical aroid with deeply lobed and fenestrated foliage, notable for its robust growth habit and dramatic architectural presence. Prized for indoor and conservatory cultivation as a statement houseplant.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Calcium oxalate crystals in sap and leaves cause oral and throat irritation, burning sensation, and difficulty swallowing if ingested.', false, NULL, true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central America', 300, 150, false, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/34838026/square.jpg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/34838026/medium.jpg', true, 206269, 206269, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera tenuis', 'Monstera tenuis', 5.5, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; causes oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs if ingested.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings; do not allow to dry completely.', 60, 80, 'Intermediate', 'A rare tropical aroid with slender stems and deeply lobed foliage, displaying fenestration on mature leaves. Prized by collectors for its elegant, minimalist aesthetic and air-purifying qualities.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Calcium oxalate crystals cause oral irritation and burning sensation if ingested; skin contact may cause mild irritation.', false, NULL, true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central America', 200, 60, true, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/14946322/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/14946322/medium.jpeg', true, 431332, 431332, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera spruceana', 'Monstera spruceana', 6.0, 7.5, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Sap and tissues contain calcium oxalate crystals, causing oral and gastrointestinal irritation if ingested. May cause drooling, difficulty swallowing, and mouth pain in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings. Reduce frequency in winter. Ensure pot has drainage holes to prevent root rot.', 65, 85, 'Intermediate', 'A rare tropical aroid with deeply pinnatifid (feathered) leaves, distinct from the fenestrated Monstera deliciosa. Prized by collectors for its dramatic foliage and climbing or trailing growth habit, suitable as a houseplant in warm, humid environments.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Sap may irritate skin and mucous membranes. Ingestion of tissue causes oral pain, drooling, and gastrointestinal upset.', false, NULL, true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Tropical South America (Amazon Basin)', 200, 120, true, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/190931867/square.jpeg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/190931867/medium.jpeg', true, 465977, 465977, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Diervilla rivularis ''Morton'' SUMMER STARS', 'Mountain bush honeysuckle', 6.0, 7.5, false, '{"Stem Cuttings",Division,Seeds}', true, '{"id": 2475, "genus": "Diervilla", "family": "Caprifoliaceae", "hybrid": null, "variety": null, "cultivar": "Morton", "authority": null, "other_name": [], "subspecies": null, "common_name": "mountain bush honeysuckle", "default_image": null, "scientific_name": ["Diervilla rivularis ''Morton'' SUMMER STARS"], "species_epithet": "rivularis"}', '2026-06-02 15:24:55.77787+00', NULL, 'Average', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Check soil at 5 cm depth; water when soil feels dry to touch. Prefers consistent moisture during growing season but tolerates dry periods once established.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A compact deciduous shrub with striking golden-yellow foliage and small tubular flowers that transition from coral-red buds to warm yellow blooms throughout summer and fall. Extremely hardy and low-maintenance, ideal for borders, mass plantings, and wildlife gardens.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, true, 'Late Summer – Autumn', true, 'Summer – Fall', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy}', 'Eastern North America', 90, 120, false, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/395713914/square.jpeg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/395713914/medium.jpeg', true, 52758, 52758, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera dissecta', 'Monstera dissecta', 6.0, 7.5, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings. Water when the surface feels dry to the touch.', 60, 85, 'Intermediate', 'A tropical aroid featuring deeply dissected, fenestrated foliage that resembles intricate lacework. Less vigorous than Monstera deliciosa but prized for its unique leaf morphology and compact growth habit, making it an elegant choice for indoor collections.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes mouth and throat irritation, swelling of lips and tongue, and difficulty swallowing. Sap may irritate skin.', false, NULL, true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Slow', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central and South America', 150, 90, true, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/182665810/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/182665810/medium.jpeg', true, 518377, 518377, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera acacoyaguensis', 'Monstera acacoyaguensis', 6.0, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings; reduce frequency in cooler months.', 60, 85, 'Intermediate', 'A rare, vining aroid endemic to Mexico with deeply lobed, leathery foliage and slower growth than Monstera deliciosa. Prized by collectors for its unique fenestrated leaves and architectural climbing habit.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Calcium oxalate crystals cause oral and throat irritation, burning sensation, and difficulty swallowing if ingested. Sap may irritate skin and eyes.', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Slow', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Mexico (Chiapas)', 180, 60, true, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/355038441/square.jpeg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/355038441/medium.jpeg', true, 276915, 276915, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera filamentosa', 'Monstera filamentosa', 6.0, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings; do not allow the root ball to dry completely.', 60, 85, 'Intermediate', 'A climbing aroid with slender stems and distinctively elongated, deeply lobed or fenestrated leaves with characteristic thread-like extensions (filaments). Slower-growing and less vigorous than Monstera deliciosa, it is prized by collectors for its unique leaf morphology and elegant growth habit.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Calcium oxalate crystals cause oral and esophageal irritation if ingested; sap may irritate skin and mucous membranes.', false, NULL, true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Slow', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central America', 200, 60, true, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/118027761/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/118027761/medium.jpeg', true, 952574, 952574, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Digitalis ferruginea', 'Rusty foxglove', 6.0, 7.5, true, '{Seeds}', true, '{"id": 2481, "genus": "Digitalis", "family": "Plantaginaceae", "hybrid": null, "variety": null, "cultivar": null, "authority": null, "other_name": [], "subspecies": null, "common_name": "rusty foxglove", "default_image": {"license": 4, "small_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2481_digitalis_ferruginea/small/28498161102_19346c2956_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=5753f8fe7f03d2a5d880a7e5ef7a11961d766592021cd4598f05a43f735c4b18", "thumbnail": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2481_digitalis_ferruginea/thumbnail/28498161102_19346c2956_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=e0a446c76743a03ce9783a5af4d100d6314a890c051198ed45853ea0c852e2e2", "medium_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2481_digitalis_ferruginea/medium/28498161102_19346c2956_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=c36193ada68f755bcf7535ae1e1f5f85ba6cbd5609fe73414ff0245ecdf8237d", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/", "regular_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2481_digitalis_ferruginea/regular/28498161102_19346c2956_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=0be52ee2f5c74857e548457acf0844f463cedc36f4554c5e7aff9222536915dd", "license_name": "Attribution License", "original_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2481_digitalis_ferruginea/og/28498161102_19346c2956_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=05d4a1c3935d8f91e6f1b690dcf724644aab4d74e969a95968d74ec13ba0440f"}, "scientific_name": ["Digitalis ferruginea"], "species_epithet": "ferruginea"}', '2026-06-02 01:40:30.724592+00', 'All parts contain cardiac glycosides; ingestion causes severe gastrointestinal distress, cardiac arrhythmias, and potentially fatal toxicity in pets.', 'Average', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Biennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings; keep consistently moist during growing season but do not waterlog.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A hardy biennial foxglove with distinctive rusty-brown tubular flowers densely packed on tall spires, reaching 60–120 cm. Prized as a cottage garden plant for its dramatic late-spring to early-summer blooms and architectural foliage.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'All plant parts contain cardiac glycosides (digitoxin and related compounds); ingestion causes severe gastroenteritis, arrhythmias, and can be fatal. Skin contact may cause dermatitis in sensitive individuals.', true, 'Summer', true, 'Late Spring – Early Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy}', 'Central and Southern Europe', 120, 45, false, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/86817375/square.jpeg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/86817375/medium.jpeg', true, 335863, 335863, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera membranacea', 'Monstera membranacea', 5.5, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Sap contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings; do not allow the plant to dry out completely. Check soil moisture at surface level regularly.', 60, 80, 'Intermediate', 'A rare tropical aroid with thin, deeply lobed or fenestrated leaves that are noticeably membranous in texture. It is a vining epiphyte that climbs and trails, prized by collectors for its delicate and ornamental foliage, though it requires stable humidity and indirect light to thrive indoors.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Sap and plant tissues contain calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes mouth and throat irritation, burning sensation, and difficulty swallowing. Skin contact may cause mild irritation.', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Moderate', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Peaty,Rich}', 'Central and South America', 150, 80, false, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/218966844/square.jpg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/218966844/medium.jpg', true, 952582, 952582, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Agave americana', 'American century plant', 6.0, 8.5, true, '{"Offset Separation",Seeds}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 01:14:33.679222+00', 'Leaves contain saponins and oxalates; ingestion causes gastrointestinal upset, drooling, and vomiting in cats and dogs. Contact with sap may cause skin irritation.', 'Minimum', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Let soil dry completely between waterings. Check soil at 5–7 cm depth; water only when bone-dry.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A dramatic succulent rosette with thick, waxy, grey-green leaves edged in sharp spines, capable of reaching massive proportions over decades. A slow-growing architectural plant prized for xeriscaping and bold foliage impact, though it requires well-draining soil and intense light.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'Leaves contain saponins and oxalates; ingestion causes burning sensation in mouth and throat, nausea, and vomiting. Sap and sharp leaf margins pose contact irritation and laceration hazards.', true, 'Spring – Summer', true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Slow', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Sandy,Poor}', 'Central Mexico (Sonoran and Chihuahuan deserts)', 200, 300, false, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/333174371/square.jpg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/333174371/medium.jpg', true, 64103, 64103, 'species');
