b to small tree native to North American wetlands, characterized by grey-brown bark, oval leaves with prominent veining, and catkin-like male flowers. Valued for nitrogen-fixing root nodules, wildlife habitat provision, and erosion control in riparian zones.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, true, 'Late Summer – Autumn', true, 'Spring', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{}', 'North America, particularly northeastern and central regions', 800, 600, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/2261216/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/2261216/medium.jpg', true, 75377, 75377, 'species');
