uous shrub with arching branches bearing fragrant, deep purple flower spikes that attract butterflies and pollinators. ''Groovy Grape'' is a bred cultivar selected for intense colour and smaller stature, making it ideal for gardens and containers.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, true, 'Late Summer – Autumn', true, 'Summer – Early Autumn', 'Fast', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy}', 'Central and Western China', 150, 120, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/87998902/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/87998902/medium.jpg', true, 75916, 75916, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Forsythia', 'Forsythias', 6.0, 8.0, false, '{"Stem Cuttings",Seeds}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 14:53:26.005375+00', NULL, 'Average', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings during the growing season. Water deeply in spring and early summer; reduce watering in autumn and winter.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A vigorous deciduous shrub celebrated for its profuse bright yellow flowers that bloom in early spring before leaf emergence. Highly ornamental and widely planted as a landscape specimen or hedge, Forsythia demands minimal maintenance and thrives in diverse soil conditions.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, true, 'Late Summer – Autumn', true, 'Early Spring', 'Fast', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Sandy}', 'Eastern Asia (China, Korea, Japan)', 300, 300, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/1181774/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/1181774/medium.jpg', true, 60580, NULL, 'genus');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera adansonii adansonii', 'Monstera adansonii adansonii', 6.0, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Sap contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral irritation, drooling, and swelling of mouth and throat in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings. Check soil moisture at the surface; water when dry to touch.', 60, 80, 'Beginner', 'A compact tropical climbing aroid with distinctive perforated leaves, smaller than its Monstera deliciosa cousin. Prized for easy care, air-purifying qualities, and dramatic fenestrated foliage that develops as the plant matures.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Sap and leaves contain calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral pain, swelling, and difficulty swallowing. Skin contact may cause mild irritation.', false, NULL, true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central and South America, West Indies', 180, 120, true, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/105213838/square.jpeg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/105213838/medium.jpeg', true, 1152461, 206267, 'subspecies');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Gleicheniaceae', 'Forked ferns', 5.5, 7.0, false, '{}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 14:53:26.005375+00', NULL, 'Frequent', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Keep soil consistently moist but not waterlogged; check at the surface daily. Spores require high humidity and moist substrate for germination.', 70, 95, 'Advanced', 'Primitive ferns with characteristic forked or dichotomous fronds, native to tropical and subtropical regions worldwide. Gleicheniaceae members are ancient lineage ferns prized by collectors for their unique morphology and exacting cultivation requirements.', 'Indoor', true, false, NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Slow', 'High', '{Peaty,Well-draining,Moisture-retaining}', 'Tropical and subtropical regions worldwide, including Central and South America, Africa, Asia, and Oceania', NULL, NULL, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/4657/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/4657/medium.jpg', true, 52493, NULL, 'family');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Bromus inermis', 'Smooth brome', 6.0, 7.5, false, '{Seeds,Division}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 14:53:26.005375+00', NULL, 'Minimum', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Check soil moisture at the root zone (5–10 cm depth). Allow soil to dry moderately between waterings; established plants are drought-tolerant once rooted.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A hardy perennial cool-season grass with fine, soft leaf blades and an extensive rhizomatous root system. Widely cultivated for pasture, hay, and erosion control in temperate regions.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, true, 'Summer', true, 'Late Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Poor}', 'Central Asia, North America (naturalized)', 120, NULL, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/449379438/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/449379438/medium.jpeg', true, 75903, 75903, 'species');
