_image/2105_cornus_alba_prairie_fire/medium/20239995739_5a10229602_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260606%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260606T071215Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=926b6a92df2ec61d525dcd716dd7f554d77786fd168afc9e4bc27b98d6e25d04", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/", "regular_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2105_cornus_alba_prairie_fire/regular/20239995739_5a10229602_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260606%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260606T071215Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=45fc93dd72f33b14641bc4538cfaf940310a06bd98019023e26a58497f7569c3", "license_name": "Attribution-ShareAlike License", "original_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2105_cornus_alba_prairie_fire/og/20239995739_5a10229602_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260606%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260606T071215Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=9d22c015e44b50f5b2f176164ce204a736d32716fa7b414b4f8dba4384c16395"}, "scientific_name": ["Cornus alba ''Prairie Fire''"], "species_epithet": "alba"}', '2026-06-06 07:12:15.89575+00', NULL, 'Average', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Check soil moisture at 5 cm depth; water when dry to touch. Prefers consistently moist but well-drained soil, especially during establishment and active growth.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A deciduous shrub prized for its vibrant red winter stem colour and compact growth habit. ''Prairie Fire'' is a hardy cultivar of Tatarian dogwood, featuring cream and green variegated foliage in summer that deepens to burgundy-red tones in autumn before leaf drop, revealing brilliant coral-red stems throughout winter.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, true, 'Late Summer – Autumn', true, 'Late Spring – Early Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Moisture-retaining}', 'Siberia, Russia, and northern China', 180, 150, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/75344741/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/75344741/medium.jpg', true, 124879, 124879, 'species');
