', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A hardy perennial cultivar of purple coneflower with distinctive white-blushed pink petals and orange-red central cone. Drought-tolerant and attracts pollinators, making it ideal for naturalized gardens and borders.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, false, NULL, true, 'Summer – Early Autumn', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Sandy,Loamy}', 'North America', 75, 45, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/433818/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/433818/medium.jpg', true, 48627, 48627, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera adansonii klotzschiana', 'Monstera adansonii klotzschiana', 6.0, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Calcium oxalate crystals cause oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs if chewed or ingested.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings. Check moisture by inserting finger at soil surface.', 60, 80, 'Beginner', 'A compact trailing aroid with small ovate leaves featuring natural fenestration, prized as a low-maintenance houseplant for shelves and hanging planters. Tolerates moderate indoor conditions and grows steadily in indirect light.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Calcium oxalate crystals cause oral burning, swelling of lips and tongue, and gastrointestinal upset if raw plant material is ingested. Sap may irritate skin and eyes on contact.', false, NULL, true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central and South America (Mexico to Panama)', 180, 60, true, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/119769431/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/119769431/medium.jpg', true, 952715, 206267, 'subspecies');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Monstera adansonii blanchetii', 'Monstera adansonii blanchetii', 6.0, 7.0, true, '{"Stem Cuttings","Air Layering"}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:51:39.681918+00', 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings. Check soil moisture at the surface; water when dry to touch but before the soil becomes completely dry.', 60, 80, 'Beginner', 'A compact, slow-growing tropical aroid with small heart-shaped leaves and distinctive fenestrations (natural holes), prized for its manageable size and trailing habit. Excellent for indoor plant collections and hanging baskets.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Contains calcium oxalate crystals; ingestion causes oral and gastrointestinal irritation, burning sensation in the mouth, and throat discomfort.', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Slow', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central and South America', 60, 45, true, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/179347783/square.jpeg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/179347783/medium.jpeg', true, 962402, 206267, 'subspecies');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Abelia schumannii', 'Abelia schumannii', 6.0, 7.5, false, '{"Stem Cuttings",Seeds}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 03:39:40.778285+00', NULL, 'Average', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings during the growing season.', 40, 60, 'Intermediate', 'A semi-evergreen to deciduous shrub with slender, arching branches and small tubular flowers that bloom in summer to autumn. Valued for its elegant habit, fragrant blooms, and ornamental value in temperate gardens.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, true, 'Autumn – Winter', true, 'Summer – Autumn', 'Moderate', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central China', 250, 200, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/570171171/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/570171171/medium.jpg', true, 1269377, 1269377, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Euonymus fortunei', 'Fortune''s spindle', 6.0, 7.5, false, '{"Stem Cuttings",Division}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 14:53:26.005375+00', NULL, 'Average', '{part_shade,full_shade,filtered_indirect}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings; do not allow complete drying.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A hardy, adaptable evergreen shrub or groundcover with small ovate leaves, often variegated with white or yellow margins. Prized for low-maintenance foliage and tolerance to diverse growing conditions, it is ideal for borders, hedging, and indoor container cultivation.', 'Both', false, false, NULL, true, 'Autumn – Winter', true, 'Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy}', 'Eastern and central China, Japan', 90, 150, false, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/28139660/square.jpeg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/28139660/medium.jpeg', true, 130893, 130893, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Duranta erecta', 'Skyflower', 6.0, 7.5, true, '{"Stem Cuttings",Seeds}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 14:53:26.005375+00', 'Berries and leaves contain saponins and other compounds that may cause gastrointestinal upset if ingested by dogs or cats.', 'Average', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings during growing season; reduce frequency in winter.', 40, 70, 'Intermediate', 'A tropical shrub with slender, arching stems and small, delicate lavender-blue flowers followed by distinctive golden-yellow berries. Prized for ornamental foliage and prolific summer blooms, it is commonly grown indoors in containers or outdoors in warm climates.', 'Both', true, true, 'Berries and foliage contain saponins; ingestion may cause gastric irritation, nausea, or diarrhoea. Skin contact may cause mild irritation in sensitive individuals.', true, 'Summer – Autumn', true, 'Spring – Summer – Autumn', 'Fast', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central and South America (Mexico to Brazil)', 200, 150, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/16323821/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/16323821/medium.jpeg', true, 162153, 162153, 'species');
