l-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/315_laburnum_x_watereri_pendulum/medium/Laburnum_x_watereri_Vossii_0zz.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T151135Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=46a6c0ec65f62b12f2bd7c3008303a6f308075d2ccea262aa8a0ddab185114a6", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en", "regular_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/315_laburnum_x_watereri_pendulum/regular/Laburnum_x_watereri_Vossii_0zz.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T151135Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=e9ec6ef0a6b3a6cf4d71b6290b5c441b19ec1289026509e26c5c81a6ac1ade85", "license_name": "Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported (CC BY-SA 3.0)", "original_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/315_laburnum_x_watereri_pendulum/og/Laburnum_x_watereri_Vossii_0zz.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T151135Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=8bb49e966b4d9a227c429499243830619a8711096b811794e499091fee461e38"}, "scientific_name": ["Laburnum x watereri ''Pendulum''"], "species_epithet": null}', '2026-06-02 15:11:36.5959+00', 'All parts, especially seeds and seedpods, contain cytisine alkaloid and are highly toxic to dogs, cats, horses, and livestock. Ingestion causes severe gastrointestinal distress, tremors, and potentially fatal cardiac arrhythmias.', 'Average', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 3–4 cm of soil to dry between waterings during the growing season. Reduce frequency in winter.', 40, 60, 'Intermediate', 'A deciduous ornamental tree with graceful drooping branches and cascades of brilliant golden-yellow pea-like flowers in late spring. Highly valued in temperate gardens for dramatic weeping habit and long flowering chains.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'Seeds and seedpods contain cytisine, a toxic alkaloid. Ingestion causes severe nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, tremors, and potentially fatal cardiac effects. Children and adults should never consume any part of the plant.', true, 'Summer – Early Autumn', true, 'Late Spring – Early Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Sandy}', 'Garden hybrid (Laburnum alpinum × Laburnum anagyroides); parent species native to Central and Southern Europe', 600, 500, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/12186994/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/12186994/medium.jpg', true, 128549, 128549, 'hybrid');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Securigera varia', 'Purple crownvetch', 5.5, 7.5, true, '{Seeds}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 04:17:00.91919+00', 'Contains cardiac glycosides and potentially hepatotoxic alkaloids; ingestion by livestock or pets may cause gastrointestinal upset, cardiac arrhythmias, and hepatic damage. All plant parts are toxic.', 'Minimum', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings; this drought-tolerant perennial prefers drier conditions once established.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A hardy leguminous perennial with delicate pink to purple clustered flowers and fine feathery foliage, widely used for soil stabilisation, erosion control, and wildlife habitat. Extremely low-maintenance and drought-tolerant once established.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'Contains cardiac glycosides and potentially hepatotoxic compounds; ingestion may cause gastrointestinal upset, cardiac effects, and hepatic injury. All plant parts pose a risk if consumed.', true, 'Summer – Autumn', true, 'Late Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Sandy,Loamy,Poor}', 'Mediterranean Basin and Central Asia', 60, 45, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/34301/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/34301/medium.jpg', true, 127186, 127186, 'species');
