/2773_epipremnum_aureum/medium/2560px-Epipremnum_aureum_31082012.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260604%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260604T015033Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=116407cc41f39df8e5b1e1bd19c783a6df27cc1841a69c7fb084a203a65e014a", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en", "regular_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2773_epipremnum_aureum/regular/2560px-Epipremnum_aureum_31082012.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260604%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260604T015033Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=b823aa8a07be776f711ae8b03452b2a18f4feaa9b20b7ba1dfd5e065f459203e", "license_name": "Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported (CC BY-SA 3.0)", "original_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2773_epipremnum_aureum/og/2560px-Epipremnum_aureum_31082012.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260604%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260604T015033Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=5551b61b6a4d19a85a9364824d52fdd9f6fd501a026840d35634e82cf5a3fccf"}, "scientific_name": ["Epipremnum aureum"], "species_epithet": "aureum"}', '2026-05-31 00:46:12.714868+00', 'Oxalate crystals in sap cause oral irritation, drooling, and difficulty swallowing in cats and dogs. Mild gastrointestinal upset may follow ingestion.', 'Average', '{"part shade","full shade"}', 'Perennial', 'Vine', 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings. In low light or cool conditions, extend drying period to 5 cm.', 50, 80, 'Beginner', 'A vigorous tropical aroid with heart-shaped, glossy leaves that mature to a golden-yellow variegation. Highly adaptable, air-purifying, and ideal for hanging baskets or climbing support; tolerates low light and neglect.', 'Indoor', true, true, 'Oxalate crystals cause oral and throat irritation if ingested. Sap may trigger skin sensitivity in sensitive individuals.', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Fast', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Southeast Asia (Solomon Islands)', 200, 100, true, 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/100110119/square.jpg', 'https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/100110119/medium.jpg', true, 69223, 69223, 'species');
