9fa_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260530%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260530T193033Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=22698edc73fe1c0c78a1d52a0382db15db2c4676817c3a1aaa21050e0c3b1a5b", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/", "regular_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/569_aesculus_woerlitzensis/regular/8695236245_99090599fa_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260530%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260530T193033Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=c221b1aad1db82427e55b9c5ff6559a974731d64913bd8097c5d748613191a46", "license_name": "Attribution License", "original_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/569_aesculus_woerlitzensis/og/8695236245_99090599fa_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260530%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260530T193033Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=0bb51824991da961410c408d669446b02ac05bea15d21af1966bd637abadef51"}, "scientific_name": ["Aesculus woerlitzensis"], "species_epithet": "woerlitzensis"}', '2026-05-30 19:30:34.808866+00', 'All parts of the plant, particularly seeds and sprouts, contain aesculin and other toxic saponins. Ingestion can cause gastrointestinal upset, drooling, vomiting, diarrhea, and in severe cases, muscle weakness or paralysis in dogs, cats, and horses.', 'Average', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 5 cm of soil to dry between waterings during the growing season. In dormancy, reduce watering significantly.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A medium-sized deciduous tree with palmately compound leaves and upright panicles of pale yellow or creamy flowers in spring, followed by smooth capsular fruits. Valued for ornamental landscaping in temperate climates and noted for vibrant autumn foliage.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'Seeds, bark, and sprouts contain saponins and aesculin. Ingestion can cause gastroenteritis, tremors, and in severe cases, paralysis. Skin contact with raw seeds may cause minor irritation.', true, 'Autumn', true, 'Spring', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central Europe (Anhalt region, Germany)', 800, 600, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/566121938/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/566121938/medium.jpg', true, 1501540, 1501540, 'hybrid');
