dramatic form and autumn colour. Slow-growing and long-lived, it serves as a focal point in large gardens and landscapes.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, true, 'Autumn', true, 'Spring', 'Slow', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Europe (temperate deciduous forests)', 800, 600, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/608828197/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/608828197/medium.jpg', true, 54227, 54227, 'species');
INSERT INTO public.cached_botanical_records (scientific_name, common_name, ideal_min_ph, ideal_max_ph, is_toxic_to_pets, propagation_methods, is_ai_enriched, raw_api_payload, cached_at, toxicity_notes, watering, sunlight, cycle, plant_type, check_depth_description, ideal_humidity_min, ideal_humidity_max, care_difficulty, description, placement, is_tropical, is_toxic_to_humans, human_toxicity_notes, produces_fruit, fruit_season, produces_flowers, flowering_season, growth_rate, maintenance_level, preferred_soil_type, native_region, max_height_cm, max_spread_cm, air_purifying, thumbnail_url, regular_url, thumbnail_fetched, inat_taxon_id, inat_species_id, inat_rank) VALUES ('Adansonia digitata', 'African baobab', 6.0, 7.5, false, '{Seeds}', true, NULL, '2026-06-08 15:02:20.60003+00', NULL, 'Minimum', '{full_sun}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow soil to dry completely between waterings. Check soil at 5–10 cm depth; water only when bone dry.', 30, 60, 'Advanced', 'A massive deciduous tree with a swollen trunk and sparse, digitate foliage, native to African savannas. Prized for drought tolerance and distinctive silhouette; produces edible, nutrient-dense fruit and fragrant flowers.', 'Outdoor', true, false, NULL, true, 'Late Summer – Autumn', true, 'Spring – Early Summer', 'Slow', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Sandy,Poor}', 'Sub-Saharan Africa, particularly savanna and semi-arid regions', 2000, 1500, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/249827419/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/249827419/medium.jpeg', true, 81500, 81500, 'species');
