e but tolerates some drought once established.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A delicate, fine-textured perennial native to southeastern North America with feathery, thread-like foliage and tiny white to pale pink flowers that attract pollinators. Prized for its airy, ornamental foliage and resilience in naturalized garden settings.', 'Outdoor', false, false, NULL, true, 'Autumn', true, 'Summer – Autumn', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Sandy}', 'Southeastern United States (Coastal Plains and Piedmont regions)', 150, 90, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/13817971/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/13817971/medium.jpg', true, 131154, 131154, 'species');
