st but never waterlogged soil.', 40, 60, 'Intermediate', 'A deciduous to semi-evergreen shrub renowned for fragrant clusters of pink, purple, or white flowers appearing in late winter to early spring, often before leaves emerge. Valued for ornamental beauty and powerful, sweet fragrance; produces small red berries in summer.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'All parts are toxic. Berries and sap are caustic; ingestion causes severe burning sensation in mouth and throat, followed by gastrointestinal distress. Skin contact may cause irritant dermatitis. Avoid handling without gloves.', true, 'Summer', true, 'Late Winter – Early Spring', 'Slow', 'Medium', '{Well-draining,Loamy}', 'Europe and temperate Asia', 150, 120, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/76021443/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/76021443/medium.jpeg', true, 133034, 133034, 'species');
