before complete drying. Boxwood prefers consistently moist but well-draining soil.', 40, 70, 'Beginner', 'A compact evergreen shrub with tiny bright green leaves, ''Apple Green'' is prized for ornamental hedging, topiary, and formal gardens. Hardy and adaptable, it tolerates shearing and maintains dense, attractive foliage year-round.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'Ingestion of leaves or berries causes nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain. Skin contact is generally safe.', true, 'Autumn', true, 'Spring', 'Slow', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'East Asia (Japan, China, Korea)', 120, 150, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/436143681/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/436143681/medium.jpeg', true, 208757, 208757, 'species');
