sys.com/perenual/species_image/2488_digitalis_purpurea_candy_mountain/medium/51288444040_2a7d785cb7_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=9b2902b3f48ff18b6d04370195c9a69dee62444018d974117a0404ab43786148", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/", "regular_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2488_digitalis_purpurea_candy_mountain/regular/51288444040_2a7d785cb7_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=20a35abeb9b683a859a449fb03f73d16179e1e730058d2cbfad90649aa6e152e", "license_name": "Attribution License", "original_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2488_digitalis_purpurea_candy_mountain/og/51288444040_2a7d785cb7_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=d3743eb71b05bc398e8bfa82f1193611f39f1b1beadcd1f65ab54489ddba0885"}, "scientific_name": ["Digitalis purpurea ''Candy Mountain''"], "species_epithet": "purpurea"}', '2026-06-02 01:40:30.850613+00', 'All parts are highly toxic. Contains cardiac glycosides (digitoxin, digoxin). Ingestion causes severe gastrointestinal distress, cardiac arrhythmias, and potentially fatal heart failure in pets and humans.', 'Average', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Biennial', NULL, 'Keep soil consistently moist during the growing season. Check soil 1 cm deep; water when soil surface feels slightly dry. Reduce watering in winter dormancy.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A vibrant biennial foxglove cultivar displaying densely-packed spires of rose-pink to magenta tubular flowers on compact, sturdy stems. Ideal for cottage gardens, borders, and cut arrangements; attracts pollinators but requires careful handling due to extreme toxicity.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'All parts contain cardiac glycosides (digitoxin, digoxin). Ingestion causes severe nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, irregular heartbeat, and potentially fatal cardiac arrest. Skin contact with sap may cause dermatitis. Never handle without gloves; wash hands thoroughly after contact.', true, 'Summer – Early Autumn', true, 'Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Western and Southwestern Europe', 80, 45, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/179728943/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/179728943/medium.jpeg', true, 53983, 53983, 'species');
