', 'A compact garden mum cultivar producing bronze-colored daisy-like flowers in autumn. Prized for seasonal colour, long bloom duration, and reliable garden performance with minimal fuss.', 'Both', false, true, 'Sesquiterpene lactones may cause mild dermatitis on skin contact or gastrointestinal upset if ingested. Generally low toxicity concern in ornamental use.', false, NULL, true, 'Autumn – Early Winter', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'East Asia (China, Korea, Japan)', 45, 50, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/236151541/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/236151541/medium.jpeg', true, 53806, 53806, 'hybrid');
