'Minimum', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 3–4 cm of soil to dry between waterings. This drought-tolerant species prefers drier conditions.', 30, 60, 'Beginner', 'A hardy perennial herbaceous plant with finely divided, silvery-green aromatic foliage. Artemisia vulgaris is prized for its ornamental texture, medicinal properties, and tolerance of poor, dry soils. Often used in herbal preparations and as a garden specimen plant.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'Contains thujone and other volatile compounds. Ingestion of excessive amounts can cause nervous system effects, including tremors and convulsions. Essential oil is particularly concentrated and dangerous; internal use should be avoided or undertaken only under professional guidance.', false, NULL, true, 'Summer – Early Autumn', 'Fast', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Sandy,Poor}', 'Temperate Eurasia and North Africa', 150, 90, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/46355424/square.jpeg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/46355424/medium.jpeg', true, 52856, 52856, 'species');
