023_asparagus_densiflorus/medium/49289066276_4bbe4e5b94_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260606%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260606T071214Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=dddcab19cba6374a5938e8bb0dfa167b1c6a56ebdeab1053abacccce2af8828c", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/", "regular_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/1023_asparagus_densiflorus/regular/49289066276_4bbe4e5b94_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260606%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260606T071214Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=7593d4008358197ae154a51c3f8a8ae416068a22f994d84c6c72a6eeb2bffa99", "license_name": "Attribution-ShareAlike License", "original_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/1023_asparagus_densiflorus/og/49289066276_4bbe4e5b94_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260606%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260606T071214Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=1da5be9334997e4293f0fcc7678269627bdd6204cdba0f63a02ec08391e68a51"}, "scientific_name": ["Asparagus densiflorus"], "species_epithet": "densiflorus"}', '2026-06-06 07:12:14.727507+00', 'Berries and roots contain saponins; ingestion by pets can cause gastroenteritis and diarrhea.', 'Average', '{filtered_indirect,part_shade}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings; do not allow the soil to dry completely as the plant prefers consistently moist but not waterlogged conditions.', 40, 60, 'Beginner', 'A delicate, feathery-leaved evergreen perennial with bright green needle-like foliage and small white flowers followed by red berries. Prized as an ornamental houseplant and trailing specimen for its soft, decorative appearance and low maintenance requirements.', 'Both', false, true, 'Berries contain saponins and may cause mild gastric upset if ingested in quantity. Sap may irritate sensitive skin.', true, 'Summer – Autumn', true, 'Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'South Africa', 60, 90, true, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/15087224/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/15087224/medium.jpg', true, 127598, 127598, 'species');
