species_image/2495_digitalis_thapsi_spanish_peaks/medium/21530257614_6528992ba9_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=23460f4b11d7b1bc48587873fa6de40afeb471689cf0359aa3ab08de07fc8993", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/", "regular_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2495_digitalis_thapsi_spanish_peaks/regular/21530257614_6528992ba9_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=0e43b493061fd4e93416d2736fb153b8d8796133490d2617ec2cd96cfea99be4", "license_name": "Attribution License", "original_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/2495_digitalis_thapsi_spanish_peaks/og/21530257614_6528992ba9_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260602%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260602T014030Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=d88c9e20096db5b6deb826d3724701f5104fb089ee7865e24cc0a8f52e67fef1"}, "scientific_name": ["Digitalis thapsi ''Spanish Peaks''"], "species_epithet": "thapsi"}', '2026-06-02 01:40:30.948785+00', 'All parts contain cardiac glycosides (cardenolides). Ingestion causes severe gastrointestinal distress, cardiac arrhythmias, and potentially fatal heart failure in dogs, cats, and livestock.', 'Minimum', '{full_sun,part_shade}', 'Biennial', NULL, 'Allow soil surface to dry between waterings; this drought-tolerant Mediterranean species dislikes prolonged moisture. Check at top 2–3 cm; water when dry.', NULL, NULL, 'Beginner', 'A short-lived biennial foxglove native to the Spanish Sierra forming compact rosettes of silvery-green woolly foliage topped with dense spires of pale yellow flowers. Notable for drought tolerance and architectural presence in Mediterranean or xeriscaping gardens.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'All parts are poisonous; cardiac glycosides can be absorbed through skin and are fatal if ingested. Handling requires gloves; never consume any part.', true, 'Summer – Autumn', true, 'Late Spring – Summer', 'Moderate', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Sandy,Poor}', 'Sierra Nevada, southern Spain', 60, 45, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/248190729/square.jpg', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/248190729/medium.jpg', true, 342133, 342133, 'species');
