W%2F20260607%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260607T104019Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=339e1149cd8a75210d0a94b3c9fa1a402375a5986f3285a46eba105d44ce6093", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/", "regular_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/image/upgrade_access.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260607%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260607T104019Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=339e1149cd8a75210d0a94b3c9fa1a402375a5986f3285a46eba105d44ce6093", "license_name": "CC0 1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0) Public Domain Dedication", "original_url": "https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/image/upgrade_access.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260607%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260607T104019Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=339e1149cd8a75210d0a94b3c9fa1a402375a5986f3285a46eba105d44ce6093"}, "scientific_name": ["Helleborus hybridus ''Blue Lady''"], "species_epithet": "hybridus"}', '2026-06-07 10:40:20.160858+00', 'All parts contain cardiac glycosides and saponins. Ingestion by dogs and cats causes gastrointestinal upset, drooling, vomiting, and diarrhea. Skin contact may cause dermatitis in sensitive individuals.', 'Average', '{part_shade,filtered_indirect}', 'Perennial', NULL, 'Allow top 2–3 cm of soil to dry between waterings during growing season. Keep consistently moist but not waterlogged in spring and early summer; reduce frequency in autumn and winter dormancy.', 40, 60, 'Intermediate', 'A winter-blooming perennial with nodding blue-tinged flowers and deeply lobed evergreen foliage. Prized for early-season color when few other plants flower, and suited to woodland gardens and shaded borders.', 'Outdoor', false, true, 'All plant parts contain cardiac glycosides and ranunculin. Ingestion causes severe gastrointestinal irritation, excessive salivation, and abdominal pain. Sap and plant material may cause contact dermatitis and skin sensitization in sensitive individuals.', true, 'Late Spring', true, 'Winter – Early Spring', 'Slow', 'Low', '{Well-draining,Loamy,Rich}', 'Central and Southern Europe', 45, 50, false, 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/491949/square.JPG', 'https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/491949/medium.JPG', true, 795141, 795141, 'hybrid');
